  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I like VR Chat Plus, a great way to support DEVs and I like the benefits, but the price charged is in US Dollars, they haven't made the purchase based on each country yet. I'm from Brazil, for us 1 dollar is worth 5.60 times our money, that is, VR Chat Plus, for us, costs R$: 56.00. That's more than any subscription, Netflix, HBO, Prime, Disney+, etc. and really hard to keep up for 90% of gamers in third world countries. Steam does this for games, each country has a price, making it possible for Brazilian players, for example, to buy games. By lowering the price to make sense with each coin, you'll earn less dollar profit, but you'll have a lot more purchases, recurring subscriptions, and encouraging players to stay in the game. I will support VR Chat Plus, but only for a month, as this game definitely deserves it, but it is completely impossible to maintain this at the moment.",
